# Configuration

Configuration values stored in the configuration file provide defaults for matching flags throughout the application.
Use the commands below to manage these values.

## Configuration file location

By default, the configuration file is stored in the operating system's user configuration directory, under `{{ .ApplicationName }}/config.yaml`:

| Platform | Default path |
| --- | --- |
| Linux | `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/{{ .ApplicationName }}/config.yaml`, or `~/.config/{{ .ApplicationName }}/config.yaml` when `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` is not set |
| macOS | `~/Library/Application Support/{{ .ApplicationName }}/config.yaml` |
| Windows | `%AppData%\{{ .ApplicationName }}\config.yaml` |

Use the global `--config <path>` flag to choose a different file:

```sh
{{ .DefaultsCommand }} list --config /path/to/config.yaml
```

Run `{{ .DefaultsCommand }} list` to see the actual configuration file path in use.

## Managing configuration

- [`{{ .DefaultsCommand }} set <key> <value>`]({{ .DefaultsCommandLink }}_set): Set a configuration value.
- [`{{ .DefaultsCommand }} get <key>`]({{ .DefaultsCommandLink }}_get): Get configured values.
- [`{{ .DefaultsCommand }} list`]({{ .DefaultsCommandLink }}_list): List configured values and documented keys.
- [`{{ .DefaultsCommand }} describe <key>`]({{ .DefaultsCommandLink }}_describe): Show detailed documentation for a configuration key.
- [`{{ .DefaultsCommand }} unset <key>`]({{ .DefaultsCommandLink }}_unset): Remove configured values.
